NS", "ai_region": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_org": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_summary": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "duplicate": false}, {"article_id": "fd8136ca6c6775838daff40b1523ffd4", "link": "https://en.prnasia.com/story/547140-0.shtml", "title": "China's Latest AI Model Brings General-Purpose Agentic Capability to Edge Devices at a Lower Cost", "description": "BEIJING , Sept. 8, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- ModelBest, a leading AI startup from China, released an open-source language model named MiniCPM5-2B for edge devices lately on September 9th , in collaboration with OpenBMB open-source community. Alongside the model weights, the team released its full-stack technical suite\u2014including datasets, training recipes, and reinforcement learning infrastructure\u2014marking a major leap forward in model intelligence density and training efficiency. Despite packing just 2 billion parameters, MiniCPM5-2B natively supports tool calling, deep search, code generation, and multi-step reasoning, pioneering the deployment of general-purpose agentic capabilities directly on edge devices. In evaluations by Artificial Analysis , MiniCPM5-2B clinched the #1 spot on the Intelligence Index among open-source models under 4 billion parameters. It also scored 20 on the Agentic Index \u2014which gauges an AI's autonomous task-execution capability\u2014significantly outpacing its peers in the sub-4B category. This breakthrough spotlights a paradigm shift in AI development: rather than aggressively scaling parameter counts, boosting \"intelligence density\" allows resource-constrained devices to deliver powerhouse performance within minimal compute, memory, and power envelopes. This approach accelerates the transition of advanced AI from centralized clouds to everyday edge hardware. The practical value of this architecture has already been proven across diverse real-world edge scenarios. Powered by MiniCPM5-2B, end-users and enterprises can seamlessly run document processing, data synthesis, code generation, and multi-turn complex Q&A locally on PCs, smartphones, robotics, and IoT hardware. Shifting compute to the edge not only safeguards user privacy and data sovereignty, but also dramatically slashes latency, cloud API costs, and infrastructure dependency. Unlike conventional \"weights-only\" releases that function as black boxes, ModelBest and OpenBMB have fully open-sourced their end-to-end pipeline across data curation, pre-training, and alignment. This radical transparency equips global researchers and developers with a reproducible blueprint to fine-tune, build, and deploy specialized edge applications. To date, downloads across ModelBest's MiniCPM family have surpassed 50 million . By sharing models, methodologies, frameworks, and raw recipes, ModelBest is deepening its commitment to the global open-source ecosystem\u2014democratizing high-efficiency, lightweight, and deployable edge AI worldwide.", "content": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "keywords": ["pdt", "iot", "afi", "cpr"], "creator": ["cision pr newswire"], "language": "english", "country": ["laos", "united arab emirates", "china", "timor-leste", "qatar", "romania", "philippines", "saudi arabia", "afghanistan", "turkmenistan", "armenia", "tajikistan", "uzbekistan", "india", "turkey", "bhutan", "syria", "azerbaijan", "pakistan", "yemen", "hong kong", "bangladesh", "brunei", "bahrain", "singapore", "vietnam", "macau", "taiwan"], "category": ["technology", "top"], "datatype": "pressrelease", "pubDate": "2026-09-09 06:25:00", "pubDateTZ": "UTC", "fetched_at": "2026-09-09 06:54:55", "image_url": null, "video_url": null, "source_id": "en_prnasisa", "source_name": "Pr Newswire Apac", "source_priority": 4111305, "source_url": "https://en.prnasia.com", "source_icon": "https://i.newsdata.io/en_prnasisa.png", "sentiment": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PROFESSIONAL AND CORPORATE PLANS", "sentiment_stats": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PROFESSIONAL AND CORPORATE PLANS", "ai_tag": "ONL